From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:07:07 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] main: add --flash-info-json FILE

--flash-info output is for humans, and scripts using it to identify a
flash need a stable format. --flash-info-json implies --flash-info and
also writes a versioned JSON document to FILE ("format":
"openFPGALoader-flash-info", "version": 1) with one entry per flash:
JEDEC ID fields, database/JEP106 names, size and its source, unique ID
{state: read|blank|none, value, bits, opcode} and the decoded SFDP.

FILE is removed at start and only written, through a temporary file
and rename, when every flash access succeeded: an existing FILE and a
zero exit status mean the content was really read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F2L6L5SJYvbBUUt4DinjGC
